meta {
  name: ListAccounts
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{bffGrpc}}
  method: /dop.bff.v1.IdentityService/ListAccounts
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {}
  ]
}

docs {
  The same surface as REST, another transport — and the same code underneath: there
  is a parity test in dop-api that breaks if the two ends diverge.

  Unlike the CORE's gRPC, here the identity comes from the TOKEN, in the
  `authorization` metadata, exactly as in REST. There is no CallContext in the body.

  This is the call made BEFORE there is an active account — `x-account-id` may go
  empty.
}
